course: dictionary
lesson: 7128
title: Penalty: a punishment or a free shot
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so check the clues around them. «He went in goal and saved a penalty» is about a football match, because goal and saved are clues. Here, a penalty is a free shot at goal.
explain: Outside sport, a penalty is a punishment for breaking a rule or a law. Libraries and parking offices charge penalties, often as money called a fine. Ask yourself: is this sentence about a game, or about breaking a rule?
explain: Look for the phrases that often go with the word, such as «take a penalty», «score a penalty» and «pay a penalty». Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: A penalty is a punishment for breaking a rule or a law.
fact: In football, a penalty is a shot at goal from a spot near the goal, given because the other team broke a rule.
fact: «Penalties» is the plural of penalty.
fact: In rugby union, a penalty goal is worth 3 points.
fact: In 2022, Argentina beat France on penalties after a 3–3 draw in the final in Qatar.
exercise: «Then he went in goal for the lunchtime match, dived full length and saved a penalty.» What is a penalty in this sentence? | A type of goalkeeper glove | A lap of the pitch | *A free shot at goal, given after a rule was broken | A punishment paid in money for being late
exercise: The library says, «You must pay a penalty for a late book.» What does penalty mean? | A prize for reading lots of books | A kind of book cover | *A punishment for breaking a rule | A free shot at goal
exercise: Which word tells you that this sentence is about a sports match? «Argentina beat France on penalties after a 3–3 draw in the final.» | *Draw | Fine | Library | Parking
test: A player has to take a penalty. What does take a penalty mean? | Pay money to the library | *Shoot at goal from the penalty spot after a rule was broken | Run around the pitch twice | Hide behind the goal
test: Leo says penalty always means a shot in football. What is the best reply? | *No, it can also mean a punishment for breaking a rule | Yes, and it is always a goal | Yes, that is the only meaning it has | No, it means a prize for winning
exam: «Kiran was fined, and the parking office added a penalty to his bill for breaking the rule.» What does penalty mean here? | A type of car part | *A punishment for breaking a rule | A free shot at goal | Money that is a gift for good driving
